      </header>

      <!-- ------------------------------------------------------- what it does -->
      <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="what">
        <span class="node" data-i="02" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="sec-head">
          <h2 id="what">Set it once. It <span class="em">keeps up</span>.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="claims">
          <div class="claim reveal">
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="15" cy="15" r="10.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" />
              <path d="M15 9v6.4l4.2 2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round" />
            </svg>
            <h3>New records, on your schedule</h3>
            <p>On arrival, hourly, daily, or only when you tap. Per destination, not one global switch.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="claim reveal">
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="5.5" y="7.5" width="19" height="15" rx="3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" />
              <path d="M9 12h9M9 15.5h12M9 19h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round" />
              <path d="M7.5 19h9.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="1 2.6" />
            </svg>
            <h3>A file, not a feed</h3>
            <p>NDJSON, JSON, CSV or Metrics JSON. Deletions travel as tombstones instead of quietly vanishing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="claim reveal">
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M5 15h7M18 15h7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round" />
              <circle cx="15" cy="15" r="3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" />
              <path d="M15 5v4M15 21v4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="1 3" />
            </svg>
            <h3>One failure stays local</h3>
            <p>Every destination carries its own cursor, so a broken one can’t block or skip the others.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- --------------------------------------------------------------- how -->
      <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="how">
        <span class="node" data-i="03" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="how">
          <div>
            <div class="sec-head" style="margin-bottom:0">
              <h2 id="how">How do I export my Apple&nbsp;Health data?</h2>
              <p>
                Four steps, about two minutes. Hozz never guesses a destination for you, so nothing
                is sent until step four.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="count"><b>475</b> <span>XCTest tests behind it</span></p>
          </div>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li class="reveal">
              <h3>Add a destination</h3>
              <p>Your Mac on the local network, a folder in Files, Home Assistant, a URL, or an MQTT broker.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="reveal">
              <h3>Choose the Health types</h3>
              <p>
                <code>heartRate</code>, <code>sleepAnalysis</code>, <code>stepCount</code>,
                <code>vo2Max</code> — a handful or the lot.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li class="reveal">
              <h3>Send a test batch</h3>
              <p>Watch it land before you trust it. Testing is a step, not an afterthought.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="reveal">
              <h3>Pick a schedule and walk away</h3>
              <p>New records go out from then on. Shortcuts and a home-screen widget report the last sync state.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ------------------------------------------------------ destinations -->
      <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="dest">
        <span class="node" data-i="04" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="sec-head">
          <h2 id="dest">Where it <span class="em">sends</span></h2>
          <p>Five places, all of them yours. Hozz runs no server of its own.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tbl-scroll reveal">
          <table>
            <caption class="sr-only">Hozz export destinations and how each one delivers data</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Destination</th>
                <th scope="col">How it gets there</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                destinations.map((d) => (
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="row">{d.name}</th>
                    <td>
                      {d.detail}
                      <span class="mono">{d.mono}</span>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="sub">Four formats</h3>
        <ul class="fmts">
          <li class="fmt reveal">
            <b>NDJSON</b>
            <span>The default. Streamable, and lossless for encoded fields.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="fmt reveal">
            <b>JSON</b>
            <span>The same records, as one document.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="fmt fmt-lossy reveal">
            <b>CSV</b>
            <span>Metadata and nested workout detail don’t fit a grid. Hozz says so rather than pretending.</span>
            <span class="tag">Lossy on purpose</span>
          </li>
          <li class="fmt reveal">
            <b>Metrics JSON</b>
            <span>The shape Home Assistant takes.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mono" style="margin-top:0.95rem">
          Deterministic encoding — byte-identical output regardless of locale or time zone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------- anchors -->
      <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="dur">
        <span class="node" data-i="05" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="sec-head">
          <h2 id="dur">It can repeat&nbsp;work. <br />It <span class="em">can’t skip</span> a&nbsp;record.</h2>
          <p>
            No date-window watermarks. Hozz holds an opaque anchor per type and only advances it
